```

```mdl
decision D-72: The canvas's plus sits in each empty cell next to the cards, or in the centre cell of an empty map, faint until pointed at, and opens a menu of New feature and Add existing feature, which place the feature in that cell. Placing it first fixes every card where it is drawn, since a new card changes the automatic layout's extent and would shift the cards around that cell. The canvas shows even when the spec holds no features. Fills in [D-66].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.9]
  why: Only the button takes the pointer, so the empty cells still pan and select; one button per cell with a menu keeps the grid quiet.
  rejected:
    - A plus shown only while the pointer is over a cell, which needs the cells to take the pointer and so stops panning from them.
    - Two buttons per cell, which doubles the marks on the grid.
```

```mdl
