```mdl
decision D-129: A task in review satisfies the tasks that depend on it, so dependents start while the person who answers for it has not yet signed off.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
```

```mdl
decision D-130: A sub-task filed under a delegated task, naming no assignee or delegate of its own, takes the parent's person assignee and no delegate. Fills in [D-125].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-128
  why: The person who answers for the tree is what makes the sub-task's finish wait on sign-off. Copying the delegate wrote half a claim: a chat delegate's checklist never listed the task, and a finished parent's session got new work.
