  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-134
```

```mdl
decision D-139: An agent claim on a step nobody answers for takes the person who answers for its tree's root, before the person the claim names; the claim cascade then carries that person to the tree. Fills in [D-135].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  why: Asked of the claimed step alone, the rule kept the session's person on an unowned step of someone else's tree, so one unit of work answered to two people.
```

```mdl
decision D-140: A step answers to its own person, else the nearest person up its tree. One `Task` helper owns that rule, and creating a task, an agent's claim, the claim cascade and a session's question each store its result on the step.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [Task]
```

```mdl
decision D-141: A sub-task filed with no assignee takes the person its parent answers to (`Task.answerer`), whether or not the tree is delegated; one filed with a delegate takes that person over one the caller names. Fills in [D-140].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-137
  why: Asked only under a delegated parent, a step two levels down had no person and closed without review.
```

```mdl
decision D-142: An agent claim takes the person the claimed step answers to, so an owned middle step wins over an unowned root; the claim cascade gives each member with no person the nearest one up its own tree, and the claim's person only where there is none. Fills in [D-140].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-139
