```mdl
decision D-145: An agent claim writes the person only on a step with no person of its own; a step that has one is left unwritten. A claim that also re-parents the step takes the person of the tree it moves into. Fills in [D-142].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  why: Writing the same person back on every claim raced a person's reassignment made on another replica, and a re-parenting claim read the old tree while its cascade wrote the new one.
