  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-5.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-201: Every CodeMirror editor in a project that edits shared text shows the other peers' carets. A plain string field shows them too, edited in place through an accessor on the live object, with no `Text` object or schema change.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.13, F-5.9]
```

```mdl
decision D-202: The editors with carets are a spec's text, the feature sections embedded in it (the feature's description), the overview's Notes and the agent's instructions. The project's description is a plain text area, not a CodeMirror editor, so it shows no carets. Fills in [D-201].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.13, F-5.9]
  why: These are the CodeMirror editors a project's views mount over shared text. A task's description is left out because it commits through `UpdateTask` on blur to write the task's history, which editing in place would bypass.
  rejected:
    - Turning the project's description into a markdown editor so it carries carets, which changes how the field looks and behaves.
```

```mdl
decision D-203: QA-9 checks carets in the overview's Notes between two peers, the host's caret set before the guest opens the project, automated by a collaboration e2e spec. Fills in [D-201].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-9, F-5.9]
  why: Notes is on the Overview of a project just made from the Default template, so the test needs no setup beyond creating it, and the late joiner is the case that failed before the awareness fix.
```

```mdl
decision D-204: QA-10 walks two peers through every editor with carets ([D-202]) in one take, recorded side by side by an autocue flow. Fills in [D-201].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-10, F-5.9]
  why: QA-9 automates the Notes alone; the instructions, the spec's prose and a feature's description need a spec with the Software package, so they are covered by a recorded walkthrough rather than another e2e test.
```

```mdl
decision D-205: Every collaborative text field in a project that takes comments also shows the other peers' carets.
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.13, F-5.9]
```

```mdl
decision D-206: The editors with carets are the project's name and description, a spec's text in either of its views, the feature sections embedded in it (the feature's name, description and requirement rows), the overview's Notes and the agent's instructions. Each collaborative string is its own awareness channel, and a spec's two views share one. Fills in [D-201] and [D-205].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-202
  affects: [F-4.13, F-5.9]
  why: These are the fields comments anchor into, plus the instructions, which already had carets. The project's name and description and a feature's fields are now collaborative strings edited in place, so they take the carets through the same binding. A spec's name and description, which the overview's Specs rows edit, are plain fields that take no comments, so they show no carets.
```

```mdl
decision D-207: QA-10 walks two peers through every editor with carets ([D-206]) in one take, adding the project's name and description and a feature's name and requirement to its steps. The two feature fields are split across peers so each field's caret shows only in that field. Fills in [D-205].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-204
  affects: [QA-10, F-4.13, F-5.9]
  why: A recorded walkthrough already covers the editors that need a spec with the Software package; the new caret sites sit in the same views, so they join the same take rather than a separate test.
```

```mdl
decision D-208: QA-9 is automated inside the document-caret collaboration test, over its invitation, rather than by a test with an invitation of its own.
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [QA-9]
```

```mdl
decision D-209: QA-9 starts once the peers share the space and both have checked the document: the host makes the project with the document, before the invitation, and each peer then opens it. The late joiner stays the document's to check. Fills in [D-208].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-203
  affects: [QA-9]
  why: A project made after the document check did not open on the host. Made first, it sits in its own section, so the guest's document list and the host's first object stay as the document steps expect.
```

```mdl
decision D-210: The Specs tab always shows the spec's text. Every other view of a spec moves to its companion, in three tabs this plugin owns: Structure, Decisions and Review. A plugin adds a view to one of them, and the tab switches between its views. Replaces the view toggle of [D-65] and [D-100].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-100
  affects: [F-4.7, F-4.8]
  rejected:
    - Views in both the Specs tab and the companion, which leaves a reader two places to look for the same thing.
```

```mdl
decision D-211: `ProjectCapabilities.SpecView` gains `group`, the tab it is one of, and stays the one registry of views. `SpecSession` holds what a spec's editor and its views share: the view each tab shows, the evidence the Review tab opened, the selections, the diff mode, and the open editor, which a view scrolls to an item. A tab's toolbar ends with the `ProjectSurface.SpecToolbar` surface, where the plugin that knows a spec's source draws it, and `ProjectSurface.SpecCompanion` draws a tab for a plank whose subject is not the spec, such as a feature's level. Fills in [D-210].
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.8]
  why: The editor and the views can be in different plugins and on different planks, so the state they share belongs to the plugin that owns both seams; plugins never import each other's components.
  rejected:
    - A registry per tab, which makes a plugin with views in several tabs contribute to several capabilities.
```

```mdl
decision D-212: QA-6 walks a spec through its companion tabs, and the autocue flow `spec-companion` records it, so the move of [D-210] has a demo a reviewer can watch.
  date: 2026-11-05
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-213: A project's companion tabs follow the spec its Specs tab shows, read from the project's view state, as a spec's own tabs follow its dialects. It carries out plugin-code's D-95 beside a project.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.8]
  why: The project offered every group any spec could use, so a video script kept a Review tab with nothing in it.
