```mdl
decision D-214: A companion view that reads any dialect belongs to this plugin: Definitions, Related, At cursor, the Ledger and Review.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6, F-7, F-8]
```

```mdl
decision D-215: Review is generic: a spec of any dialect is offered it. The code a verdict cites stays with the software dialect.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-216: F-6, F-7 and F-8 take plugin-code's F-25 (without the Video package, now plugin-video's), F-26, and F-24.6 and F-24.7. The views get the checkout through `ProjectCapabilities.SpecSourcesProvider`, and a package styles its field values on cards through `SpecPackage.facts`. Fills in [D-214] and [D-215].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.4, F-6.7]
  why: The views read the checkout through plugin-code's hooks, and only plugin-code knows a file service or a GitHub source.
```

```mdl
decision D-217: A spec that names no dialects is read with the core and changelog blocks only, not as software. A bundled spec names its dialects. Fills in [D-214].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.6, F-4.3]
  why: A software fallback in a generic view made every dialect-less spec look like software, which F-4.3 already rules out.
```

```mdl
decision D-218: A spec's blocks are drawn as forms over their kinds' schemas, read from the `ext` blocks of its dialects and its own. The text stays the only store, and the editor has preview, readonly and source views as a Markdown document does.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.14]
  why: Feature objects copied what the text already says, and the copies drifted. Edits through the form keep the text's comments and alignment.
```

```mdl
decision D-219: A form's title, prose and prose fields are editors bound to their source range, so carets and comments show inside them as they do in the text.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.14]
  why: Feature fields showed carets on main, and the inline form had to keep parity.
```

```mdl
decision D-220: A numbered kind's id is a stable random key and its `F-n` label is positional, drawn and never written. Slash commands write the key and only the required fields, then focus the block's form. Replaces the numbering of [D-82].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.10]
  why: A positional id renumbered on every insert, breaking comments, links and task relations that cited it.
```

```mdl
decision D-221: Specs stay flat on the project. The nav tree nests a spec beneath every spec whose `Ref<spec>` field cites it, read from the text and cached per spec; a cycle stops before a spec repeats.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.6]
  why: A breakdown is a `spec:` field on the parent `feat` block, so nesting follows the text instead of an owner link.
```

```mdl
decision D-222: The generic block operations `GetSpecBlocks`, `SetSpecBlock` and `DeleteSpecBlock` replace the per-feature operations for every dialect.
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.15]
  why: With blocks in the text, one set of operations checked against each kind's schema covers every kind.
```

```mdl
decision D-215: A spec's carets show in its text and in each block form drawn in it; a feature is a `feat` block of the text, drawn as one of those forms. Amends [F-4.13].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.13]
```

```mdl
decision D-216: A block form is laid out compactly, as the feature section was: a header row of label, title and choice tags; a row per field with its name inline; a line per keyed entry and per map row; empty fields and actions only while focused; foldable to its header. Amends [F-4.14].
  date: 2026-11-06
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-4.14]
  why: The standard form gives every field a labelled well, so a block of three lines took a screen. The form should read close to its source while keeping fields typed and checked.
  rejected:
    - The standard form with the compact presentation, which still boxes each map row and each list.
```
